  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "How to read this dashboard",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 4
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "**Three acts, top to bottom:** is the data valid (the contract), did the inputs move, did the model get worse. The last row, collapsed, holds the slices, the diagnosis and the alerts. **Weeks are simulated** (1 to 16) and are plotted by week number on the x axis, not as time. Inputs and score describe week N the day it runs. **Performance and slices need labels, which arrive a week late**, so they show week N only after week N+1 has run (week 9's labels never arrive: its batch was blocked). Alerts repeat from week 5 because the drift baseline stays the champion's training window until a new model is promoted."
   },
   "id": 1
  },
